/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (IN REVENUES For all revenue sources surveyed, among respondents who have that specific source, the majority \(65%-85% of respondents\) reported that revenue amounts have either not changed or decreased, pulling the summary trend below 3.00. Despite this, the trend for total revenues is flat overall. Aside from the 20% of respondents whose total revenues are unchanged, there is nearly an even split among respondents who reported decreases \(36% of respondents\) and those who reported increases \(42% of respondents\). )
/E (IN REVENUES For all revenue sources surveyed, among respondents who have that specific source, the majority \(65%-85% of respondents\) reported that revenue amounts have either not changed or decreased, pulling the summary trend below 3.00. Despite this, the trend for total revenues is flat overall. Aside from the 20% of respondents whose total revenues are unchanged, there is nearly an even split among respondents who reported decreases \(36% of respondents\) and those who reported increases \(42% of respondents\). )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
