/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (FUND DEVELOPMENT Of all the surveyed subcomponents in the Operations and Governance area, the strongest increased trend is in fund development \(4.02; increased for 71% of respondents\). Investing in reporting to funders and government also increased significantly \(3.89; increased for 62% of respondents\). Likely, increased investment is in response to revenues not keeping up with expenses and increased demand and the need to look for new sources of revenue.)
/E (FUND DEVELOPMENT Of all the surveyed subcomponents in the Operations and Governance area, the strongest increased trend is in fund development \(4.02; increased for 71% of respondents\). Investing in reporting to funders and government also increased significantly \(3.89; increased for 62% of respondents\). Likely, increased investment is in response to revenues not keeping up with expenses and increased demand and the need to look for new sources of revenue.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
