/T (PLANNING AND GENERAL GOVERNANCE The strongest increased trends in governance-related subcomponents are strategic/scenario/succession/crisis planning \(3.79; increased for 61% of respondents\), and general board governance \(3.74; increased for 59% of respondents\). )
/E (PLANNING AND GENERAL GOVERNANCE The strongest increased trends in governance-related subcomponents are strategic/scenario/succession/crisis planning \(3.79; increased for 61% of respondents\), and general board governance \(3.74; increased for 59% of respondents\). )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Overall, across all subcomponents surveyed, more respondents report increasing their investments than those that reported no change, while few reported decreases. The survey did not inquire about the immediate reasons behind these investments, during a time of flat revenues. More research is needed to understand why organizations are choosing to strengthen internal systems and core capacities and whether this is driven by the expectations and standards of interest parties such as staff, clients, board members, funders, or the public. It is reasonable to assume that increased investment in fund development is in response to usual revenues not keeping up with expenses and demands for increased services. )
/E (Overall, across all subcomponents surveyed, more respondents report increasing their investments than those that reported no change, while few reported decreases. The survey did not inquire about the immediate reasons behind these investments, during a time of flat revenues. More research is needed to understand why organizations are choosing to strengthen internal systems and core capacities and whether this is driven by the expectations and standards of interest parties such as staff, clients, board members, funders, or the public. It is reasonable to assume that increased investment in fund development is in response to usual revenues not keeping up with expenses and demands for increased services. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
