/T (These quotes illustrate ways that organizations are collaborating with each other to reduce costs. In the area of Programs, Services, and Activities, respondents indicated that they are increasing their investments into relationship-building, outreach, and collaborations \(3.90; increased for 78% of respondents\). Interestingly, this is not reflected in the Operations & Governance subcomponent of investing in strategic alliances, shared services, or mergers, which remained relatively unchanged \(3.63; increased for 41%\). More research is needed to explore how these two different types of activities are carried out within organizations, and how they are linked to organizational capacity. )
/E (These quotes illustrate ways that organizations are collaborating with each other to reduce costs. In the area of Programs, Services, and Activities, respondents indicated that they are increasing their investments into relationship-building, outreach, and collaborations \(3.90; increased for 78% of respondents\). Interestingly, this is not reflected in the Operations & Governance subcomponent of investing in strategic alliances, shared services, or mergers, which remained relatively unchanged \(3.63; increased for 41%\). More research is needed to explore how these two different types of activities are carried out within organizations, and how they are linked to organizational capacity. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
