<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Our survey results show that many organizations are investing more in their internal capacities, even as financial pressures mount. The most notable increase is in fund development \(4.02; increased for 71% of respondents\). Given that overall revenues remain flat, it is likely that most organizations are investing more staff time into fund development, diverting it from other needs.  )
/E (Our survey results show that many organizations are investing more in their internal capacities, even as financial pressures mount. The most notable increase is in fund development \(4.02; increased for 71% of respondents\). Given that overall revenues remain flat, it is likely that most organizations are investing more staff time into fund development, diverting it from other needs.  )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (It is unsurprising that non-profits are pivoting to fund development amidst increasingly difficult financial strain. With total expenses rising \(4.06; increased for 84% of respondents\) but total revenues remaining flat overall \(3.00; decreased for 36% of respondents, increased for 42% of respondents\), organizations are under pressure to intensify their search for funding and reinforce their operational supports. However, the number of unique revenue sources is also overall flat \(3.01; unchanged for 38% of respondents\), implying that more time and capacity are required for revenue sources to be successfully diversified.)
/E (It is unsurprising that non-profits are pivoting to fund development amidst increasingly difficult financial strain. With total expenses rising \(4.06; increased for 84% of respondents\) but total revenues remaining flat overall \(3.00; decreased for 36% of respondents, increased for 42% of respondents\), organizations are under pressure to intensify their search for funding and reinforce their operational supports. However, the number of unique revenue sources is also overall flat \(3.01; unchanged for 38% of respondents\), implying that more time and capacity are required for revenue sources to be successfully diversified.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
