1467 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (RECOMMENDATION Funding agreements should allow a flexible, unrestricted percentage of expenses to be allocated to administration, infrastructure, physical space, and data collection and evaluation. Currently, the percentage of allowable administrative expenses varies between 5-15% within the sector. This cap does not reflect true costs. Supporting core costs with a flexible, unrestricted percentage allows non-profits to maintain their operations. Furthermore, the provision of dedicated streams of core funding would enable non-profits to collaborate with other non-profits, and to enhance services, supports, and activities for British Columbians.  )
/E (RECOMMENDATION Funding agreements should allow a flexible, unrestricted percentage of expenses to be allocated to administration, infrastructure, physical space, and data collection and evaluation. Currently, the percentage of allowable administrative expenses varies between 5-15% within the sector. This cap does not reflect true costs. Supporting core costs with a flexible, unrestricted percentage allows non-profits to maintain their operations. Furthermore, the provision of dedicated streams of core funding would enable non-profits to collaborate with other non-profits, and to enhance services, supports, and activities for British Columbians.  )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [1]
>>
